[{"code":"record_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":28,"col":10},"end":{"line":28,"col":23}},"title":"RECORD CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`{ r | x = 1 }` changes `r` itself, but `b#Box.0` still holds the old record and\nis used whole afterwards.\n\n27|    b = apply Box r\n       ^ `b#Box.0` keeps the record here\n28|    r2 = { r | x = 1 }\n            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the record is changed in place here\n29|    ( b, r2 )\n         ^ and `b#Box.0` is used here, after the change\n\nIf the record were changed in place, `b#Box.0` would carry the new values of the\nchanged fields when it is used on line 29.\n\nTo change a copy and leave `r` as it was, copy it there:\n\n28|    r2 = { Record.copy r | x = 1 }\n\nThis is sharing the checker can see: `b#Box.0` is used whole on line 29, after\nthe change."}]
